@startuml
title SSD 3 — Conduct Consultation and Record Clinical Information (UC08)
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
actor HealthcareProfessional as Professional
participant ":System" as System
Professional -> System: recordConsultation(appointmentID, observations, diagnoses,\ntreatmentRecommendations, followUpRequirements)
alt not authorised, not found, not confirmed/arrived, duplicate, or invalid content
  System --> Professional: accessDenied / notFound / invalidState / invalidInput
else audit or commit fails
  System --> Professional: auditUnavailable / systemError
else consultation recorded
  System --> Professional: consultationID, appointmentStatus = completed
  opt medication prescribed
    Professional -> System: issuePrescription(consultationID, items)
    alt valid prescribing authority and medication items; commit succeeds
      System --> Professional: prescriptionID
    else rejected or failed
      System --> Professional: accessDenied / invalidInput / notFound / auditUnavailable / systemError
    end
  end
  opt follow-up required
    Professional -> System: searchAvailability(serviceID, professionalID?, locationID?, dateRange, specialtyID?)
    alt no eligible slots
      System --> Professional: [] — No availability
      note over Professional,System
      No follow-up is booked. Staff/patient may separately join the waiting list.
      end note
    else eligible slots exist
      System --> Professional: slots (professionalID, dateTime, locationID)
      Professional -> System: requestFollowUp(consultationID, serviceID, professionalID,\nlocationID, dateTime, referralID?)
      alt all checks including resource allocation pass
        System --> Professional: appointmentID, status = requested
      else rejected or failed
        System --> Professional: slotUnavailable / resourceUnavailable / referralRequired /\nreferralInvalid / accessDenied / notFound / invalidInput / auditUnavailable / systemError
      end
    end
  end
end
note over Professional,System
Patient is derived from consultationID, never supplied by the caller.
Prescription/follow-up failure does not undo the recorded consultation.
Follow-up is not automatically confirmed.
end note
@enduml
